A destroy that leaves threads waiting on a mutex it took away.
The thread waits on an object that is no longer live.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: thread waits on something that is neither a notification nor a mutex

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -917,7 +917,7 @@ bool sched_forget(struct obj_header *o, bool preempt)
             m->holder = 0;
             thread_settle(h);
         }
-        while (m->waiters != 0) {
+        while (m->waiters != 0 && o->type != CAP_MUTEX) {
             LOOP_PAID(sched_forget, waiter, "a thread that waited, by a call of its own");
             struct thread *t = p2v(m->waiters);
             unwait(t);
